  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "labelRecursivePatterns",
    "file": "rdkit/Code/GraphMol/SmilesParse/SmilesParse.cpp",
    "description": "`labelRecursivePatterns()` uses `std::list<SmaState> state` as a stack but pops on every `')'` without checking emptiness. Malformed SMARTS with more closing parens than pushes causes `state.pop_back()` on an empty list (UB), corrupting list internals and later triggering an invalid free in libc++ list deallocation. Crash is observed at `state.pop_back()`/list teardown, but root cause is missing balance/empty checks before stack pop in this function.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer input reaches `ParseMarvinSmartsLine()` via `M  MRV SMA` molblock property in `ParseMolBlockProperties()`, then calls `SmartsToMol()`, which first calls `labelRecursivePatterns(sma)`. A crafted SMARTS string (as in PoV) containing unmatched `)` drives the parser state machine to execute `state.pop_back()` when `state` is empty. This underflow leads to bad-free during list node handling/destruction."
  },
